# What must NOT reach the deployment. This is a different question from
# .gitignore: `profile/` is untracked but must still ship, because the scoring
# function reads it at runtime.

# Resume, cover letters, outreach drafts. Nothing in the pipeline reads these.
output/

# The local SQLite working set, kept only as a backup of the original backfill.
# Neon is the live database.
data/

# Belt and braces: the gateway key, the Neon URL and CRON_SECRET live here.
# Vercel injects the real values from project settings.
.env
.env.*

# NOTE: profile/ is deliberately absent from this list. lib/profile.ts does a
# readFileSync on profile/{summary,resume,targets}.md inside triage and score,
# so excluding it makes the nightly run die with ENOENT the first time it has a
# posting to judge — and not before, which is how it went unnoticed.
